== categories focus: input#fd-v-74-title ""
{
 "heading": "New category",
 "name": "New category",
 "text": "New category The category starts as a draft. Points of interest or routes are put in it from their editors; categories have two levels at most. Name · English(required) Applies to * Points of Interest Groups points of interest, such as Sculpture. Routes Groups routes, such as Short tours. A category in use cannot change this later. Level Top-level A main group with its own subcategories. Subcategory Sits under a top-level category of the same kind. Code: built from the title Edit code Cancel Create and open",
 "fields": [
  "input[text] \"Name · English(required)\" req=null val=\"\" ph=",
  "input[radio] \"Points of InterestGroups points of interest, such as Sculpture.\" req=null val=false ph=",
  "input[radio] \"RoutesGroups routes, such as Short tours.\" req=null val=false ph=",
  "input[radio] \"Top-levelA main group with its own subcategories.\" req=null val=true ph=",
  "input[radio] \"SubcategorySits under a top-level category of the same kind.\" req=null val=false ph=",
  "input[text] \"Code\" req=null val=\"\" ph="
 ],
 "btns": [
  "Edit code",
  "Cancel",
  "Create and open"
 ],
 "h": 636,
 "w": 576
}
